@@ -0,0 +1,32 @@
+---
+id: dl-003-hourly-rental-utc-hour-boundaries-under-24-hours-optional-hourlyprice-no-discount
+type: decision-log
+title: "Hourly rental: UTC hour boundaries, under 24 hours, optional hourlyPrice, no discount"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+<!-- decision-log body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold, setting only `id`, `title` and
+     `status` (and any `--tags` or `--set` value). Fill the required frontmatter fields and replace
+     these placeholder comments yourself; `wingfoil memory submit` then checks the required fields,
+     moves `status` forward and commits the document as you left it, naming in the commit body the
+     content it carries. -->
+
+## Context
+
+Visitors want a board for an afternoon. Rentals were whole UTC days only (dl-001).
+
+## Decision
+
+- `hourlyPrice` is optional on `Equipment`; without it the item cannot be rented by the hour.
+- A rental is hourly when it is shorter than 24 hours. Both ends must then fall on the hour in UTC
+  (so offsets such as +05:30 are refused). A rental of 24 hours or more keeps the whole-UTC-day rule.
+- The total is hours x `hourlyPrice`. The long-rental discount (dl-002) is counted in days and does not apply.
+- Hourly rentals use the same half-open periods and overlap check as day rentals, so they conflict
+  with any overlapping booking of the same item.
+- `availability` is unchanged and still takes whole days.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Totals stay integer cents. Hours are not capped to the day price, so a 23-hour rental may cost more
+than a day. Hourly availability queries would be a separate change.
